{"dur":180,"ev":[{"t":0.8,"type":"voice","id":"v01"},{"t":7.2,"type":"voice","id":"v02"},{"t":11,"type":"voice","id":"v03"},{"t":18,"type":"voice","id":"v04"},{"t":30.8,"type":"voice","id":"v05"},{"t":44.2,"type":"voice","id":"v06"},{"t":57.467,"type":"voice","id":"e1"},{"t":72.467,"type":"voice","id":"e2"},{"t":87.467,"type":"voice","id":"e3"},{"t":102.467,"type":"voice","id":"e4"},{"t":117.467,"type":"voice","id":"e5"},{"t":122.6,"type":"voice","id":"v07"},{"t":135.8,"type":"voice","id":"v08"},{"t":140.02,"type":"voice","id":"y1"},{"t":141.687,"type":"voice","id":"y2"},{"t":143.353,"type":"voice","id":"y3"},{"t":145.02,"type":"voice","id":"y4"},{"t":146.687,"type":"voice","id":"y5"},{"t":151.667,"type":"voice","id":"v09"},{"t":164,"type":"voice","id":"v10"},{"t":0.8,"type":"sub","d":5.461,"text":"When the gods and the demons churned the ocean of milk, the first thing it gave up was poison."},{"t":7.2,"type":"sub","d":2.848,"text":"Halahala: dark enough to end every world."},{"t":11,"type":"sub","d":5.77,"text":"Shiva took it in his hands, and drank it. He held it in his throat, and his throat turned blue."},{"t":18,"type":"sub","d":6.872,"text":"So he is called Neelakantha, the blue-throated one: the destroyer who saved the world from destruction."},{"t":30.8,"type":"sub","d":8.772,"text":"He is the ascetic of Mount Kailash, the first of all yogis, and the dancer whose steps undo the world, so that it can begin again."},{"t":44.2,"type":"sub","d":6.443,"text":"In the south of India, five great temples honour him as the five elements of which everything is made."},{"t":57.467,"type":"sub","d":6.792,"text":"Earth, at Kanchipuram, where he is worshipped in a lingam of sand, beneath an ancient mango tree."},{"t":72.467,"type":"sub","d":7.142,"text":"Water, at Thiruvanaikaval, where a spring rises in the sanctum, and the shrine is never fully dry."},{"t":87.467,"type":"sub","d":8.104,"text":"Fire, at Tiruvannamalai. Each year, at the festival of Karthigai, a great flame is lit on the summit of the hill."},{"t":102.467,"type":"sub","d":6.784,"text":"Air, at Srikalahasti, where a lamp in the inner shrine is said to flicker, though no wind can reach it."},{"t":117.467,"type":"sub","d":4.008,"text":"And space, at Chidambaram, where he dances as Nataraja."},{"t":122.6,"type":"sub","d":9.042,"text":"Behind a curtain there, the secret of Chidambaram is revealed: an empty space. Nothing to see, because the formless has no form."},{"t":135.8,"type":"sub","d":3.496,"text":"His mantra has five syllables, one for each element."},{"t":140,"type":"sub","d":7.26666666666668,"text":"Na. Ma. Shi. Va. Ya."},{"t":151.667,"type":"sub","d":1.663,"text":"Om Namah Shivaya."},{"t":164,"type":"sub","d":5.812,"text":"The world is painted, kept, and washed away. And the paper beneath it was always there."},{"t":0.2,"type":"sea","d":29.5},{"t":0.2,"type":"brush","d":2.8,"g":0.4,"pan0":-0.8,"pan1":0.8},{"t":0.6,"type":"brush","d":2.6,"g":0.4,"pan0":0,"pan1":0},{"t":2.6,"type":"churn","d":9.2},{"t":6.6,"type":"poison","d":5.2},{"t":11.8,"type":"gather","d":3.8},{"t":16.67,"type":"chime"},{"t":18.8,"type":"pencil","d":1.1},{"t":30,"type":"brush","d":1.2,"g":0.45,"pan0":-0.9,"pan1":0.9},{"t":30.4,"type":"wind","d":13},{"t":31,"type":"brush","d":3.2,"g":0.45,"pan0":-0.4,"pan1":0.6},{"t":35.4,"type":"brush","d":1.6,"g":0.35,"pan0":0.5,"pan1":0.7},{"t":34.8,"type":"pencil","d":1.1},{"t":43.333,"type":"brush","d":1.2,"g":0.45,"pan0":-0.9,"pan1":0.9},{"t":45,"type":"pencil","d":0.8},{"t":50.833,"type":"brush","d":0.7,"g":0.3,"pan0":-0.3,"pan1":0.2},{"t":51.667,"type":"brush","d":0.7,"g":0.3,"pan0":-0.3,"pan1":0.2},{"t":52.5,"type":"brush","d":0.7,"g":0.3,"pan0":-0.3,"pan1":0.2},{"t":53.333,"type":"brush","d":0.7,"g":0.3,"pan0":-0.3,"pan1":0.2},{"t":54.167,"type":"brush","d":0.7,"g":0.3,"pan0":-0.3,"pan1":0.2},{"t":56.667,"type":"rise","d":1.4,"k":0},{"t":57.467,"type":"pencil","d":1.2},{"t":57.667,"type":"brush","d":3,"g":0.4,"pan0":-0.6,"pan1":0.6},{"t":71.667,"typ